{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1180606-how-can-you-modify-the-chase-rules-to-allow-players-to-escape-angels-and-gods","id":1180606,"title":"How can you modify the chase rules to allow players to escape angels and gods?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-29T21:57:19-08:00","id":1180606,"title":"How can you modify the chase rules to allow players to escape angels and gods?","content":"Had a problem in the last chronicle I ran, the PCs, demons were being hunted by an angel. The problems I ran into were, the angel as an ephemeral, was easily able to locate them, I didn't see a way/reason/method to make the challenging for the angel. Once it had located them it had a massive dice pool to attack with, taking it head on wasn't a good option, but neither was running, because they couldn't outrun it, since as my understanding of the new chase rules is you add 2 attributes/skills for the dicepool, and being ephemeral that pool was always 15. I'd like to know of a good way to allow the characters to outrun angels and other &quot;god like&quot; beings. I'm thinking of scenes more like the ones with the agents in the Matrix. Agents are overwhelming, but they can escape them, cleverly perhaps even beat them (dodge this). Because this isn't really specific to demon, could be talking a true fae, or an arch mage, etc.<br /> <br /> The best I've come up with so far is that perhaps ephemeral and other 3 attribute beings can only apply one of their attributes to chase<br /> <br /> Looking for general suggestions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 01-30-2018, 01:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T22:44:04-08:00","id":1180616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1180606-how-can-you-modify-the-chase-rules-to-allow-players-to-escape-angels-and-gods#post1180606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">because they couldn't outrun it, since as my understanding of the new chase rules is you add 2 attributes/skills for the dicepool, and being ephemeral that pool was always 15</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Being ephemeral&quot; that pool is <i>unusable</i>. Ephemeral beings use single Attributes for anything that isn't a Manifestation, a Numen, an attack, or an Attribute + Attribute task, which at the very least should translate to their approach in a given turn relying on Power or Finesse with their Rank added or not added, and even that should be done with a certain amount of understood translation to and from an appropriate dicepool for characters who aren't ephemeral beings for the purposes of setting the terms for any given turn \u2014 it doesn't quite follow for a Chase where one side is ephemeral and the other isn't to invariably degenerate into whoever doesn't have the Edge losing their entire dicepool over time until they can flip the scene-framing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:06:36-08:00","id":1181000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1180606-how-can-you-modify-the-chase-rules-to-allow-players-to-escape-angels-and-gods?p=1180616#post1180616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Being ephemeral&quot; that pool is <i>unusable</i>. Ephemeral beings use single Attributes for anything that isn't a Manifestation, a Numen, an attack, or an Attribute + Attribute task, which at the very least should translate to their approach in a given turn relying on Power or Finesse with their Rank added or not added, and even that should be done with a certain amount of understood translation to and from an appropriate dicepool for characters who aren't ephemeral beings for the purposes of setting the terms for any given turn \u2014 it doesn't quite follow for a Chase where one side is ephemeral and the other isn't to invariably degenerate into whoever doesn't have the Edge losing their entire dicepool over time until they can flip the scene-framing.</div> </div> </div> </div>you know I read this, thrice, and maybe it's the alcohol, but I don't understand your suggestion. Are you saying it doesn't make sense to add power +finesse in the first place? or power + rank? for a chase roll? or what? also turned out my players were terrible at taking the edge, or using it, and my ephemeral ended up being fairly equilateral, so basically the same states power + finnesse or resistance whichever way you flipped it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:27:22-08:00","id":1181004,"title":"","content":"I think he meant that since ephemerals roll Power/Finesse + Rank where mortals roll Attribute + Skill, the angel shouldn\u2019t have had that huge a dice pool to throw around amidst a chase. And even +Rank in the dice pool isn\u2019t guaranteed since, similar to how mortals just may not have the Skill the dice pool calls for, an ephemeral might find the dice pool representing an action that isn\u2019t in its nature, thus not adding Rank to its dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-30T21:39:32-08:00","id":1181008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1180606-how-can-you-modify-the-chase-rules-to-allow-players-to-escape-angels-and-gods?p=1181004#post1181004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think he meant that since ephemerals roll Power/Finesse + Rank where mortals roll Attribute + Skill, the angel shouldn\u2019t have had that huge a dice pool to throw around amidst a chase. And even +Rank in the dice pool isn\u2019t guaranteed since, similar to how mortals just may not have the Skill the dice pool calls for, an ephemeral might find the dice pool representing an action that isn\u2019t in its nature, thus not adding Rank to its dice.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and the fact that since ephemeral beings don't have the same Traits that characters with full sheets use, any Chase where one party is an ephemeral being and the other one isn't is going to have to set the dicepool for a given turn as something that the other party cannot possibly use; this in turn would mean that, in practice, every roll made when you don't have the Edge loses 10-Again and a cumulative -1 penalty, because you cannot possibly roll Finesse + Rank as a stigmatic and the pursuing angel has no Wits + Streetwise to roll if you turn the tables.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T07:41:11-08:00","id":1181122,"title":"","content":"I think I'ms starting to see where I was screwing up, I was doing something like Finesse + Power for the angels rolls, not even Finesse + Rank. Also I wasn't applying a cumulative -1 penalty. Would you suggest using the same mechanics for &quot;Brief nightmares&quot; since a brief nightmare also doesn't have Wits or Streetwise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T12:31:00-08:00","id":1181195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1180606-how-can-you-modify-the-chase-rules-to-allow-players-to-escape-angels-and-gods?p=1181122#post1181122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'ms starting to see where I was screwing up, I was doing something like Finesse + Power for the angels rolls, not even Finesse + Rank. Also I wasn't applying a cumulative -1 penalty. Would you suggest using the same mechanics for &quot;Brief nightmares&quot; since a brief nightmare also doesn't have Wits or Streetwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>For Brief Nightmares, check if the Chase would fall under their Best At or Worst At dice pools. If neither, use the Other pool. They deliberately don't list statistics otherwise to keep things simple. I wouldn't penalize them, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-31T16:44:05-08:00","id":1181273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1180606-how-can-you-modify-the-chase-rules-to-allow-players-to-escape-angels-and-gods?p=1181122#post1181122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'ms starting to see where I was screwing up, I was doing something like Finesse + Power for the angels rolls, not even Finesse + Rank. Also I wasn't applying a cumulative -1 penalty. Would you suggest using the same mechanics for &quot;Brief nightmares&quot; since a brief nightmare also doesn't have Wits or Streetwise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Power + Finesse is an Attribute + Attribute task. Attribute + Attribute tasks are rare and the chase rules don't give any specific examples of them.<br /> <br /> I would personally assign a suitable Attribute + Skill as if adjucating a chase between two non-ephemeral characters, and then translate the angel's dice pool into the equivalent ephemeral dice pool: whichever ephemeral Attribute corresponds to the character's Attribute, and then consider whether this particular type of chase falls within the purview and nature of this angel (if it's a hunter angel it likely is), and if so, add Rank. In situations where the terms of the chase fall outside the purview, just roll the one ephemeral Attribute by itself as the base pool. This binary Rank modifier is what ephemeral entities use instead of checking for Skill ratings.<br /> <br /> So, for example, a demon flees a hunting angel with two spindly flexible legs it uses to leap long distances. The demon is caught in the open by the shore, and has to roll Strength + Athletics to outrun the angel, which the angel matches with Power + Rank. The demon thinks fast and dives over the side of a bridge, transitioning into an underwater chase. The dice pool might then become Stamina + Athletics, for argument's sake, and if the angel's configuration isn't suitable for flexible underwater movement, it may now simply be rolling Resistance as its pool. Salt to taste, but it's likely a good idea to keep that Rank modifier in mind to give your players a chance to come up with ideas to outmaneuver angels if they can infer the nature of the particular angel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T05:13:43-08:00","id":1181361,"title":"","content":"How does the cumulative -1 work? I don't recall that from the rules for chase at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T06:58:33-08:00","id":1181383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1180606-how-can-you-modify-the-chase-rules-to-allow-players-to-escape-angels-and-gods?p=1181361#post1181361\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the cumulative -1 work? I don't recall that from the rules for chase at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the Turn-By-Turn section on p85 of the ChroD corebook.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If the other side wishes to use other dice pools, they lose the 10-again quality on his roll, and suffer a cumulative -1 penalty. This penalty increases every time he uses a dice pool aside from the one dictated. He does not suffer it on turns where he has the Edge or otherwise uses the dictated dice pool, but it continues to amass if he decides not to on a future turn. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}